WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.020
We have to realize something.

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:09.630
The debate about what to do with the country
over the next four to six weeks is not primarily

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:13.620
an empirical debate about science out in public.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.820
It is not about flattening the curve.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:20.280
It's not about looking at the case fatality
rate versus the infection fatality rate or

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:21.609
anything like that.

00:00:21.609 --> 00:00:28.769
The current coronavirus debate happening in
popular culture is merely about who favors

00:00:28.769 --> 00:00:32.330
a let them die approach and who does not.

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:37.399
And increasingly, we have to accept that Republicans
are making clear that they favor a let them

00:00:37.399 --> 00:00:39.199
die strategy now.

00:00:39.199 --> 00:00:43.749
So far, it doesn't seem like the governors
of the states with a lot of protests are being

00:00:43.749 --> 00:00:45.609
influenced by the protests.

00:00:45.609 --> 00:00:47.389
That's a good thing.

00:00:47.389 --> 00:00:51.069
But it does appear that a lot of Republican
governors are starting to open things up.

00:00:51.069 --> 00:00:52.209
I'll tell you which ones.

00:00:52.209 --> 00:00:59.850
And it's important to understand that the
flattening of the curve doesn't directly save

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:05.239
lives in the sense that when you flatten the
curve, you still expect that over time, without

00:01:05.239 --> 00:01:08.979
a vaccine, the same total number of people
would become infected.

00:01:08.979 --> 00:01:14.990
It saves lives by spreading that same number
of cases out enough so that everybody can

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:19.500
get the best medical treatment possible because
the medical system isn't overwhelmed.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:24.229
And by virtue of making sure resources are
available, it saves lives.

00:01:24.229 --> 00:01:28.990
Imagine a million infections in a week versus
a million infections in a year.

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:32.670
Many more people will die with a million infections
in a week because many won't be able to actually

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:34.829
get the medical care that would be appropriate.

00:01:34.829 --> 00:01:40.729
Either way, it's a million infections, but
we want to spread those out as much as possible.

00:01:40.729 --> 00:01:45.270
Republicans are increasingly saying forget
about spreading it out, let it rip.

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:48.120
We are okay with letting them die.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.270
Florida is starting to reopen beaches.

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:54.329
Now, you might think, well, Florida must have
the virus under control, right?

00:01:54.329 --> 00:01:55.329
Very wrong.

00:01:55.329 --> 00:01:57.590
Florida has nearly 30000 cases.

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:00.000
They're in a very clear plateau.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:05.260
If you loosen guidelines during a plateau,
cases start going up again next week.

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:08.729
South Carolina is set to reopen beaches and
retail stores.

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:14.190
South Carolina, for now, fortunately, doesn't
have that many cases, by which I mean they

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:16.150
have about forty five hundred.

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:20.230
But we can expect those to start going up
once they reopen.

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:24.510
The Georgia governor camp says that businesses
like gyms, barbershops and hairstylists can

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:27.690
start opening this Friday, April 24.

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:32.680
Theaters, restaurants can follow on Monday,
April 27.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:37.680
You've got Texas Republican Gov. Greg Abbott
saying businesses in the state would start

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:41.180
to reopen next week through a series of executive
orders.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:48.689
Texas has about 20000 cases, so of course,
we can't hide in our houses forever.

00:02:48.689 --> 00:02:56.069
But this has turned into essentially a referendum
on let them die because of the constitution

00:02:56.069 --> 00:02:59.170
in some vaguely phrased terms or don't let
them die.

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:06.590
Now, during the 1918 flu pandemic, there were
instances of parts of the country ending quarantines

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:09.720
early and very quickly cases exploded.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:12.240
Look at Philadelphia as one example.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:13.689
We're already starting to see that.

00:03:13.689 --> 00:03:16.340
Look at Kentucky, for example, on Sunday.

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:22.470
Kentucky had on a percentage basis their biggest
single day increase in cases to date.

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:26.969
And what's important to understand at this
point, we've gotta understand this, guys.

00:03:26.969 --> 00:03:32.409
Even if the case numbers are low, the percentage
increases what you want to look at because

00:03:32.409 --> 00:03:39.819
the term going viral comes from viruses and
a small number of cases can still be associated

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:41.431
with a large percentage increase.

00:03:41.431 --> 00:03:46.340
And next thing you know, you've got a rapidly
increasing problem on your hands.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:52.879
Now, protests during the week have continued
to increase and not surprisingly, we won't

00:03:52.879 --> 00:03:54.939
know for 10 or 14 days.

00:03:54.939 --> 00:03:57.659
That will also lead to a spike in cases.

00:03:57.659 --> 00:04:01.810
We have Wisconsin, you might remember Wisconsin
voted on April 7th.

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:04.290
We are exactly 14 days from that election.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:06.969
And after leveling off and starting to come
down.

00:04:06.969 --> 00:04:10.569
Wisconsin is now starting to see an uptick
in cases.

00:04:10.569 --> 00:04:13.790
We'll know the full scope of that within another
couple of days.

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:14.790
This stuff is real.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:16.910
And, you know, Trump likes to call it the
invisible enemy.

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:19.140
It is invisible in a sense.

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:24.170
But you see the mass gatherings and then you
see the case numbers increase.

00:04:24.170 --> 00:04:25.910
That's not invisible.

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:26.910
So the.

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:30.810
Chatterji from Republicans is let them die
to save the economy.

00:04:30.810 --> 00:04:37.210
And we have to recognize that a widespread
pandemic will hurt the economy even more in

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.210
the long run.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:42.830
There's a number of recent papers about this
that shouldn't surprise us, though, with health

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:43.830
care.

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:47.880
For decades, the Republican strategy has been
let them die.

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:51.440
We can give everyone health care, but it would
cost too much.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:54.000
We can't afford to do that.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:59.170
So people that could be saved from a medical
perspective are going to have to die because

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:03.740
we don't want taxes to go up or whatever bill
of goods goods they've managed to sell us.

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:08.630
So we're fighting the virus and we're fighting
the disinformation and we're fighting the

00:05:08.630 --> 00:05:10.140
irresponsible actors.

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:16.970
There's a lot of fighting going on and the
numbers in another couple of weeks may look

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:19.870
very, very bad for some of these red states.

00:05:19.870 --> 00:06:29.000
I hope not, but that's what the early indicators
are showing us.

